pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Byte-identical to `substitute_degree_underflow.pbp` except that the degree is `i64::MIN + 1`
% instead of `i64::MIN`, one unit off the wrap. The substituted degree is then exactly
% `i64::MIN`, which still fits, so no contradicting row is produced and this forgery was
% refused by the UNFIXED checker too. That is what pins causation to the overflow rather than
% to "large numbers confuse the checker".
f 2;
rup 1 x2 >= -9223372036854775807 ;
red 1 ~x1 >= 1 : x1 -> 1 ;
pol 1 4 +;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 5;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
